## 1. ArmOperation.cs
The `IsResource<T>()` method at line 96 uses reflection on `typeof(T)` without annotations, causing IL2090 and IL2087.

Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]` to the generic `T` on the `IsResource<T>()` method.

Also add the same constraint annotation on both `Rehydrate<T>` (line 44) and `RehydrateAsync<T>` (line 82) methods since they call `IsResource<T>()` and `new GenericOperationSource<T>()`.

You need to add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` at the top if not already present.

The `T` constraint already has `where T : notnull`. The annotation goes on the method signature:
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull
```

For `Rehydrate<T>` and `RehydrateAsync<T>`, since they also create `GenericOperationSource<T>` which requires `PublicConstructors | NonPublicConstructors`, the annotation should be:
```csharp
[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]
```

## 2. GenericOperationSource.cs
Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]` to the class's generic parameter `T`:
